# Every audit action an `AuditLogger` collaborator declares as a constant, classified by whether the row it
# writes is the trail's own EVIDENCE THAT AN ERASURE WAS EXECUTED — the one class of row the retention prune
# may never take.
#
# The rule this file exists to enforce: evidence may not expire before the thing it attests. A
# `GDPR_SUBJECT_ERASED` row answers for a `dek_keystore` tombstone kept for ever on purpose, and
# `SubjectErasureReconciler` anti-joins the two with no date bound — so an evidence row that ages out turns
# every correctly-shredded subject into a permanent reported divergence, daily and for ever. That is the
# defect `AuditErasureEvidence` closed.
#
# What this file adds is the direction that class could not defend. Centralising the two literals made a
# DRIFTED token impossible: a rename now breaks compilation instead of silently returning a row to the sweep.
# It did nothing about a MISSING MEMBER — a third context growing a crypto-shredded subject and minting its
# own `GDPR_ACCOUNT_ERASED` with its own tombstone. Nothing pointed at `AuditErasureEvidence::ACTIONS`, so
# the prune would delete it at its level's ceiling and the reconciler built on it would report every correct
# erasure as divergence, with every gate green. The omission failed toward deletion, which is the wrong
# direction for a closed set to fail in, and every comparable closed set in this repo already had a registry.
#
# Format, one per line:
#   <ACTION_TOKEN> => evidence
#   <ACTION_TOKEN> => ordinary
#
# There is no third spelling and no default. A new token is unclassified until somebody writes the line, and
# unclassified fails the build — so the decision is made by whoever mints the action, in the diff that mints
# it, rather than inherited by whoever next reads the pruner.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT A GREEN BUILD HERE PROVES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. `make php.lint.audit-evidence` derives the universe by
# reflection — every string constant matching an action token on a class whose constructor takes
# `AuditLogger` — then checks completeness (every derived token is classified), staleness (every classified
# token still exists in the tree), and agreement in BOTH directions (`evidence` here ⇔ a member of
# `AuditErasureEvidence::ACTIONS`). Its limits:
#
#   - IT NEVER JUDGES THE CLASSIFICATION. `ordinary` over an action that really is erasure evidence passes,
#     exactly as `non-person` passes in `.person-reference-policy`. The human classifies, the automation
#     verifies. Architecture review is the only control on that direction, and it is the direction that
#     loses data, so a new `ordinary` line deserves the same scrutiny as a new `person ::` owner.
#   - IT ONLY SEES ACTIONS DECLARED AS A CONSTANT ON AN `AuditLogger` COLLABORATOR. An action passed as an
#     inline literal at the `log()` call site, read from configuration, or composed at runtime is invisible.
#     The route-derived actions are the standing example and are safe for a different reason: `AuditPolicy`
#     prefixes them `ROUTE_` unconditionally, so no user-influenced value can ever equal an exempt token.
#     A future erasure path that inlines its action instead of naming it is the shape this cannot see.
#   - IT PROVES THE TOKEN IS CLASSIFIED, NEVER THAT THE PRUNE RETAINS THE ROW. That the exemption reaches the
#     statement, and reaches it in the INNER select where it has to be, is pinned by
#     `tests/Functional/Shared/Audit/ErasureEvidenceRetentionFunctionalTest.php` against real Postgres — not
#     here, and not by any count in this file.
#   - IT SAYS NOTHING ABOUT RETENTION LENGTH. `evidence` means exempt from the sweep entirely. A bounded
#     floor — the shape `AuditErasureEvidence` weighed and declined for `GDPR_ERASURE_EXECUTED` — would need
#     its own spelling here, and adding one is a decision about data minimisation, not a spelling change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ACCESS_DENIED                  => ordinary
AUDIT_TRAIL_READ               => ordinary
BANK_ACCOUNTS_SEARCHED         => ordinary
BANK_ACCOUNTS_VIEWED           => ordinary
GDPR_ERASURE_EXECUTED          => evidence
GDPR_SUBJECT_ERASED            => evidence
INVALID_CURRENT_PASSWORD       => ordinary
PASSWORD_RECOVERY_THROTTLED    => ordinary
STORED_IDENTITY_DRIFT_DETECTED => ordinary
USER_LOCKED                    => ordinary
USER_ROLES_CHANGED             => ordinary
USER_ROLES_GRANTED             => ordinary
